<title>GERMANY: PWA H1 grp pre-tax profit slightly up. [corrected 07:47 gmt]</title>
<headline>PWA H1 grp pre-tax profit slightly up. [corrected 07:47 gmt]</headline>
<dateline>ASCHAFFENBURG, Germany 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects headline from &quot;slightly down&quot; to &quot;slightly up&quot;.)</p>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		     104     vs 103</p>
<p>    (Corrects from &quot;103 vs 104&quot; to &quot;104 vs 103&quot;)</p>
<p>    Group sales				  2,500   vs 2,700</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German paper products group is Papierwerke Waldhof-Aschaffenburg AG.</p>
<p>PWA said the 1996 profit figure included 46 million marks in proceeds from the sale of its PWA Kunstoff unit.</p>
<p>The group also said its results were also not directly comparable with year-ago levels because of the sale of its Systemform unit and the swap of Zewawell for Moelnlycke Tissue.</p>
<p>PWA said business conditions during the six-month period saw &quot;clear growth&quot; in the hygenic paper business but weak demand in the fine paper market segments that weighed on results.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
